                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "416f32ec-bb39-36d6-86dc-128c24cd0e3a",
                        "entry_id": "886b945f-ca30-3069-b888-5a6f02af1ea9",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Samen von Senfpflanzen; dient gemahlen als Basis für Speisesenf und wird auch im Ganzen als Gewürz verwendet"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "f2a9c008-a6fa-4ac6-b1ef-37dd9cfd67ce",
                                "sense_id": "416f32ec-bb39-36d6-86dc-128c24cd0e3a",
                                "text": "„Die Gurke an sich, so lernt der Besucher, ist ziemlich uninteressant. Erst blühender Dill, Pfeffer, Majoran, Bohnenkraut, Weinblätter, Senfkörner geben dem krummen Ding seinen unverwechselbaren Charakter.“"
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "b38cce51-4c39-4819-9cbd-f5c21cd40db1",
                        "source_entry_id": "886b945f-ca30-3069-b888-5a6f02af1ea9",
                        "source_sense_id": "416f32ec-bb39-36d6-86dc-128c24cd0e3a",
                        "source_sense_description": "Samen von Senfpflanzen",
                        "target_lang_word": "mustard seed",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "mustard seed",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9265e7e1-4b44-3764-834a-eb97a26e4376",
                                        "entry_id": "69cc3287-b817-3f14-9736-a13bf3d80f44",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A small, round seed of the mustard plant."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "de48fadb-e846-3c7e-87f7-21b49ba7f14e",
                                        "entry_id": "69cc3287-b817-3f14-9736-a13bf3d80f44",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A small amount."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "figuratively",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e1c3f4f6-a413-4f3f-9ce2-9313912c03d5",
                                                "sense_id": "de48fadb-e846-3c7e-87f7-21b49ba7f14e",
                                                "text": "Start with a mustard seed of irrelevant fact. Rutherford Hayes’s wife, Lucy, was the first American president’s wife to be referred to as the first lady."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a6ef5d6f-5ea4-497e-86e9-4543fdc7d927",
                                                "sense_id": "de48fadb-e846-3c7e-87f7-21b49ba7f14e",
                                                "text": "It was obvious to anybody with eyes and ears and a mustard seed of sense that Thomas had been chosen as a blunt instrument of Black oppression."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d3f1c0bd-0e21-3b75-a981-08ef8715ff45",
                                        "entry_id": "69cc3287-b817-3f14-9736-a13bf3d80f44",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Small lead shot, usually of size No. 12, used for shooting birds and other animals at close range."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "also",
                                            "attributive",
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "818b8e06-1129-40c5-b3e2-6fe49e73159c",
                                                "sense_id": "d3f1c0bd-0e21-3b75-a981-08ef8715ff45",
                                                "text": "Being myself much given to the collection of birds for scientific purposes, a line of operation, requiring, in most cases, the finest shot that can be procured, I use mustard seed habitually, and have learned, incidentally as it were, its efficacy when directed against birds which, it might be thought, could not be brought down with it."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "911557d8-a8b2-4823-8fcb-6e0181ba3a52",
                                                "sense_id": "d3f1c0bd-0e21-3b75-a981-08ef8715ff45",
                                                "text": "“ […] Much as I hated to do it, while that sow was chasing after him, I let him have it in the stern with a light load of mustard-seed shot. That combination worked!” […] The mustard-seed shot he mentions are No. 12's and the load was extremely light."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "95f7a5c1-d1b0-4044-9edc-7cd468f7a103",
                                                "sense_id": "d3f1c0bd-0e21-3b75-a981-08ef8715ff45",
                                                "text": "Hmmmm... you suppose if you miss, you might blow a 1+1/2\" hole anyway, with that rig? :) Even #9? 22rf shot (mustard seed) is supposed to be #12, not sure what that would do either. :/"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
